= Ruth Fischer Comes to Berlin

Ruth Fischer is twenty-three, a founder of the Austrian party and a ruthless speaker. She has come to Berlin with Arkadi Maslow, a Russian-born student who has read everything. They think the Zentrale talks too much. They also think a party that boycotts the unions will never lead anyone, so in Berlin, where the Left Radicals still hold the district committee, she could be useful to us.

- @berlin: Give her a post in the Berlin district.
- @distance: Keep her at arm's length.

@berlin
subtitle: Before the congress she will be on our side. After it, she may want the Zentrale.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_left = 1;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.district_berlin_loyalty += 5;
RG.setRole('fischer', 'Berlin district organiser');
!}

Within weeks Fischer is the best-known speaker in the Berlin district, and the Left Radicals find their meetings full of her supporters.

@distance
subtitle: The Zentrale does not need another faction. The Left will resent it.
on-arrival: heid_left = 2; offensive_satisfaction -= 6; lean_luxemburgist += 1

Fischer is given a desk in the women's section. She uses it to write about the Zentrale's timidity.
